James sought a compelling name for his paper assessing the impacts of climate change on GDP through a meta-analysis of 85 econometric models from 15 studies. He highlighted that his work reveals significant inequalities in these impacts across countries and emphasized the model's limitations regarding unobserved variables and adaptation. In response, I provided a list of ten title suggestions designed to encapsulate the essence of his research, with themes of inequality, climate impacts, and global GDP trends. James was encouraged to choose or refine any of the titles that resonated with him.
